// @run
// @log 7
// @log 7
// silent-class-inventory D623 (2026-08-30). `vl check` returned 0 and `vl run` printed
// `Invalid input WebAssembly code: type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)`.
//
// ITS OWN FILE, NOT A PROGRAM IN `arm-and-its-layout-twin-share-one-heap.vl`. Appended there
// the same source is a DIFFERENT program: the other five programs' declarations change what
// `{ r: null }` resolves to and it becomes `emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed
// context` — a real defect, but not this one. A witness that only reproduces alone belongs
// alone.
//
// WHAT IT PINS. `rlSig`'s heap branch is a LADDER — `rlElemStructRow` first, and when that
// answers -1 (a registered union ARM, D32's nominal floor) the concrete-VARIANT fall-through
// `rlElemVariantHeap`. Since D280 an arm whose layout a declared struct also claims takes THAT
// row's heap (`uVarHeap[vi] = sHeapIdx[uVarSTwinAt(vi)]`), so the two rows already render one
// signature and `rlTwin` already merges them onto ONE vals wrapper. `mvValsElemStructRow` is
// the PAIRWISE restatement of that signature and it mirrored only the first rung, so the map
// layer reported two wrappers where the mint had made one. Probed at the mint on this
// program: `mv0 nm=Circle rl=0 wrap=11 srow=-1 vrow=0 vhtwin=0` beside
// `mv1 nm={r:null} rl=1 wrap=11 srow=0` — one wrapper, two byte-identical 7-field map structs,
// `mkcall` typed `(func (result (ref $16)))` and `GW`'s field `(mut (ref $15))`. The rec group
// now carries ONE of them and the module is 2,928 bytes against 2,949.
//
// EVERY INGREDIENT IS LOAD-BEARING and the CARRIER is the one that names the row: `mkcall`'s
// `Map()` infers `{r: null}` at its first key write, which interns onto `Dot`'s ref-list row
// while the destination's interns onto the ARM's. Annotate either end to `{[string]: Circle}`
// and both ends name one row and the program always ran — which is why nothing before this
// reached it. Drop `type Dot`, drop `type Shape`, or make the field `r: i32` and it also ran.
// The enclosing function is SCENERY: hoisting the body out still failed, which is what
// separates this from D613 even though the two print the same validator sentence.
//
// TWO PROGRAMS. The first is the filed witness verbatim. The second is the ROUND TRIP — it
// reads the stored value back through `??`, so it fails if the merged heap is merely accepted
// by the validator rather than actually shared.
type Circle = { r: i32 | null }
type Dot = { r: i32 | null }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type GW = { g: {[string]: Circle} }
function mkcall() {
  const cc = Map()
  cc["k0"] = { r: null }
  return cc
}
function outer() {
  const wv: GW = { g: mkcall() }
  const got = (wv.g)["k0"] ?? { r: 0 }
  if got.r == null { print(7) } else { print(0) }
}
outer()

// PROGRAM 2 — the same pair with the value STORED and read back non-null, so the merge is
// graded on a hit as well as on the null the carrier's first key write inferred.
type Circle2 = { r: i32 | null }
type Dot2 = { r: i32 | null }
type Sq2 = { s: i32 }
type Shape2 = Circle2 | Sq2
type GW2 = { g: {[string]: Circle2} }
function mk2() {
  const cc = Map()
  cc["k0"] = { r: 7 }
  return cc
}
function outer2() {
  const w2: GW2 = { g: mk2() }
  const got2 = (w2.g)["k0"] ?? { r: 0 }
  if got2.r != null { print(7) } else { print(0) }
}
outer2()
